/*
 * Topics for the API reference. Each function, class and constant in
 * analog_shield.py joins one with @ingroup in its docstring or ## comment; keep the
 * table on the main page (extras/doxygen/mainpage.md) in step.
 * The topics sit under one parent topic, so the Topics list shows which file
 * they document.
 */

/**
@defgroup shield_api analog_shield.py
@brief The Analog Shield library: `import analog_shield as shield`, on top of phyduino.py.

Copy analog_shield.py to the board next to your main.py. It needs the
Phyduino Pico firmware, which has phyduino.py built in.
*/

/**
@defgroup leds LEDs
@ingroup shield_api
@brief The green (D1) and red (D2) LEDs on D6 and D5.

Each LED runs from VIO (JP3) through 1 kOhm to its pin, so it lights when the
pin is low. `green_led` and `red_led` take care of that: on() drives the pin
low. The third LED, D3 (red), is a power light on VIO and can't be switched.
*/

/**
@defgroup encoder Rotary encoder
@ingroup shield_api
@brief The rotary encoder (ENC1) on D3 and D4, and its push switch on D2.

The shield has pull-ups and RC filters on all three lines, so they are inputs
with no pull of their own and read low when closed. Pin interrupts count the
turns, so none are missed while your program does something else.
*/

/**
@defgroup temperature Temperature and amplifier
@ingroup shield_api
@brief The LMT84 temperature sensor (U1) and the TLV2472 amplifier (U2).

The chain, as on the schematic:

| Stage | Signal | Read with |
|---|---|---|
| Sensor: LMT84 (JP1 on INT) or J1 (JP1 on EXT) | SENSOR_IN, about 0.18-1.3 V | raw_sensor_volts() on A1; sensor_volts() works it out from the end of the chain |
| U2A: non-inverting amplifier with an offset | sensor * 4.35 - 0.648 V | amplifier_volts(), amplifier_gain(), amplifier_offset_volts() |
| U2B: unity-gain low-pass filter, about 10.7 kHz | OPA_OUT, 0-5 V, also on J8 pin 4 | amplifier_volts() |
| R14/R15 divider, x 0.411 | TEMP_SIG, 0-2.05 V | output_volts() on A3 (JP2 on EXT) or A0 (JP2 on INT) |

temperature() runs the whole chain backwards and converts the sensor voltage
with the LMT84's datasheet curve. The amplifier spreads about -50 to 150 °C
over the A3 input's 0-2.048 V.
*/

/**
@defgroup pot Potentiometer
@ingroup shield_api
@brief The potentiometer (RV1) on A5.

The wiper goes from 0 V to VIO (JP3). A5 is on the Phyduino's MAX11635, which
reads up to 2.048 V.
*/
